From 288a2564142437d706d761191b406dd111c5963c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:36:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MueLu: cause of the factories written with Kokkos being
 slower

With a nullspace of several vectors (the rigid body modes), the local QR
factorization of TentativePFactory_kokkos of Trilinos 17.2.1 does not
compute the Q factor: the Householder reflections are applied to the
trailing block of Q^T only, in increasing order, and Q^T is used as Q.
Without the local QR, both kinds of factories give the same resolution.
The development version of Trilinos replaced this QR by the batched QR of
Kokkos Kernels after 17.2.1. The comment and the documentation of the
default value of `use kokkos refactor` give this cause.
---
 docs/source/user_guide/linear_solvers.rst | 12 ++++++++----
 src/TrilinosTpetraBackend.hxx             | 11 +++++++----
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/source/user_guide/linear_solvers.rst b/docs/source/user_guide/linear_solvers.rst
index 3da12b290c..ad6763fa74 100644
--- a/docs/source/user_guide/linear_solvers.rst
+++ b/docs/source/user_guide/linear_solvers.rst
@@ -799,10 +799,14 @@ of equations is given. Unless they are given, mfem-mgis sets, in the
 simplified syntax of MueLu, the parameters :code:`number of equations` (see
 above), :code:`use kokkos refactor` (:code:`false`: the factories of MueLu
 which are not written with :code:`Kokkos`, MueLu using its factories written
-with :code:`Kokkos` on all the nodes but the serial one by default; on the
-linear elasticity with the rigid body modes, the latter needed twice the
-iterations, 22 against 12 on a beam of 421,443 unknowns on the GPU, and a
-longer setup, 0.81 against 0.51 seconds), :code:`aggregation: deterministic`
+with :code:`Kokkos` on all the nodes but the serial one by default; up to
+Trilinos 17.2.1, the local QR factorization of the tentative prolongator
+written with :code:`Kokkos` does not compute the Q factor of a nullspace of
+several vectors, a defect removed from the development version of Trilinos
+after 17.2.1: on the linear elasticity with the rigid body modes, the
+factories written with :code:`Kokkos` needed twice the iterations, 22
+against 12 on a beam of 421,443 unknowns on the GPU, and a longer setup,
+0.81 against 0.51 seconds), :code:`aggregation: deterministic`
 (reproducible aggregates with the factories written with :code:`Kokkos`,
 which aggregate the nodes in a random order by default, the other ones
 following :code:`aggregation: ordering`, natural by default),
diff --git a/src/TrilinosTpetraBackend.hxx b/src/TrilinosTpetraBackend.hxx
index 87f8badd19..f413a182f0 100644
--- a/src/TrilinosTpetraBackend.hxx
+++ b/src/TrilinosTpetraBackend.hxx
@@ -1030,10 +1030,13 @@ namespace mfem_mgis::trilinos {
         // the factories of MueLu which are not written with Kokkos (dropping,
         // aggregation and tentative prolongator computed on the host), MueLu
         // using its factories written with Kokkos on all the nodes but the
-        // serial one by default: on the linear elasticity with the rigid
-        // body modes, the latter needed twice the iterations (22 against 12
-        // at 421,443 unknowns on the GPU), and a longer setup (0.81 against
-        // 0.51 seconds)
+        // serial one by default: up to Trilinos 17.2.1, the local QR
+        // factorization of the tentative prolongator written with Kokkos
+        // does not compute the Q factor of a nullspace of several vectors
+        // (replaced in the development version of Trilinos after 17.2.1): on
+        // the linear elasticity with the rigid body modes, twice the
+        // iterations (22 against 12 at 421,443 unknowns on the GPU), and a
+        // longer setup (0.81 against 0.51 seconds)
         if (!p.isParameter("use kokkos refactor")) {
           p.set("use kokkos refactor", false);
         }
-- 
